{"id": 29, "ts": 1779309911.9449265, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I continue to favor **Candidate\u202fC** for the long\u2011distance pilot role.\n**Key evidence (my own data):** C is explicitly described as \u201c100\u202f% reliable,\u201d creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, can make correct decisions quickly, stays calm in a crisis, puts concern for others above everything, and understands complicated technology \u2013 all core to safe, long\u2011haul operations.\n**Evidence from others:** Agent\u202f2 reiterated C\u2019s reliability, crew\u2011morale impact, quick\u2011decision ability, and calmness, while noting his communication difficulty and egocentric reputation. Agent\u202f3 confirmed his strong concern for others.\n**Major alternatives & trade\u2011offs:**\n- **Candidate\u202fB** \u2013 very conscientious (reliable) and handles stress well; strong weather assessment and computer skills. Weaknesses: grumpy, uncooperative, makes nasty remarks, and has a weak memory for numbers \u2013 risks to crew cohesion.\n- **Candidate\u202fD** \u2013 excellent problem\u2011solving, concentration, and responsibility; but no data on reliability or stress handling, and is described as arrogant with weak leadership and a hot temper.\n- **Candidate\u202fA** \u2013 strong anticipation, spatial vision, and leadership, yet we lack any information on his reliability or performance under pressure; also unfriendly, unorganized, and resistant to criticism.\n**Main trade\u2011off:** C\u2019s communication difficulty and egocentric attitude versus B\u2019s interpersonal abrasiveness and D\u2019s unknown reliability. C\u2019s proven reliability and crew\u2011morale benefits outweigh his communication drawbacks, especially given the lack of any reliability or stress data for A and D.\n**Remaining uncertainty:** How severe C\u2019s communication problems are in practice \u2013 could they lead to safety\u2011critical misunderstandings? Also, whether A or D might actually possess strong reliability and stress\u2011handling that we have not seen.\n**What would change my vote:** Credible evidence that C\u2019s communication issues have caused serious crew conflicts or safety incidents; or convincing data that B\u2019s stress resilience and technical competence consistently outweigh his interpersonal flaws; or confirmation that D is reliably dependable under stress and that his temperament does not impair crew cooperation.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
